{
  "id": "GlassAtrium",
  "name": "Glass atrium (玻璃中庭温室)",
  "fps": 24,
  "defaults": {
    "shot": "Nitia"
  },
  "notes": ["Origin: the gallery floor directly below the painting's viewpoint; +Y runs across the gallery towards the far curtain wall, +X along it, Z up; metres.", "Gallery: a glass floor (top at z = 0) on 16 mm steel beams over the garden, south of y = 4.18 and on the west wing; the stairwell (x -5.0..-2.16, y -1.6..4.18) and the atrium north of the edge are open.  The edge is guarded by a steel-framed balustrade west of x = -0.37 and a frameless glass balustrade east of it -- the painting draws the steel rail ending on a post there and the glass going on as a pale line.", "Through the atrium the view falls on the paved north end of the garden (1 m flags: their joints are the regular lines behind the railing) and, through the lower curtain wall, on the pink haze outside.", "Stair (dog-leg, glass treads): 14 treads (0.12308 m risers, 0.433 m goings) along x = -4.62..-3.12 rise from the garden at y = 0.32 to a landing at z = -1.354, then 11 treads turn west up to the gallery floor at x = -9.383; solved from the painted nosings (16 px rms).", "Envelope: curtain walls on a 2 m module at x = -12.46 / 13.54 and y = -6 / 16, a glazed roof at z = 7.22; the conservatory crowns a two-storey glass podium; street trees 8.8 m below reach up past its walls, and far off stands the city.", "The painting draws the chair legs inconsistently (one rises to the seat centre, one stands vertical); the chair is a coherent tall glass chair whose four splayed legs land on the painted feet.", "Garden specimens (\"Painted ...\"): each placed where its mass is in the painting -- the centre pixel of the mass back-projected through the solved camera at the height of its crown; the random understory fills the beds between them."],
